Rule 1     program -> statements
Rule 2     statements -> statements statement
Rule 3     statements -> statement
Rule 4     statement -> SEQUENCE IDENTIFIER ASSIGN STRING
Rule 5     statement -> TRANSCRIBE IDENTIFIER ARROW IDENTIFIER
Rule 6     statement -> TRANSLATE IDENTIFIER ARROW IDENTIFIER
Rule 7     statement -> REVERSE IDENTIFIER ARROW IDENTIFIER
Rule 8     statement -> COMPLEMENT IDENTIFIER ARROW IDENTIFIER
Rule 9     statement -> GC IDENTIFIER ARROW IDENTIFIER
Rule 10    statement -> PRINT IDENTIFIER

Terminals, with rules where they appear

ARROW                : 5 6 7 8 9
ASSIGN               : 4
COMPLEMENT           : 8
GC                   : 9
IDENTIFIER           : 4 5 5 6 6 7 7 8 8 9 9 10
PRINT                : 10
REVERSE              : 7
SEQUENCE             : 4
STRING               : 4
TRANSCRIBE           : 5
TRANSLATE            : 6
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

